  "title": "Extract typed-I/O and provenance mechanisms from scientific workflow languages",
  "question": "What do CWL, WDL, Nextflow and Snakemake do for typed inputs/outputs and machine-readable provenance (RO-Crate-class) that this program's workflow schema currently cannot express — and is the provenance model adoptable without adopting a second runtime?",
  "answer": "CWL and WDL give a portable type algebra (File/Directory/scalars/arrays/structs) and CWL adds checksummed File objects with secondaryFiles. This schema can only name string ports (command-center/schema/workflow.schema.json:47-48). RO-Crate 1.1 + Workflow Run RO-Crate supply machine-readable provenance as JSON-LD documents with CreateAction graphs — adoptable as an export, not as a second orchestrator. Nextflow process I/O is channel/dataflow and is the inseparable control: adopting it imports the Nextflow runtime. Snakemake's .snakemake/metadata store is a second inseparable layout. SUCCESS:RES-0064 in the receipt AND a mechanism table with a runtime-entanglement verdict per row and one inseparable example",
